course: dictionary
lesson: 6649
title: Numb: no feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Numb means a part of your body cannot feel anything. It can be from cold, like fingers after a snowball fight, or from medicine, like a tooth at the dentist. «For a filling the dentist numbs the tooth with an injection.» Here numbs is a verb: to numb is to make a body part lose feeling.
explain: Numb can also describe feelings. «She was numb with shock when she heard the news.» Shock or very sad news can leave you feeling nothing for a while, so numb describes a person, not just a hand or a tooth.
explain: Use the context to choose the right meaning. If the sentence is about cold, medicine or a leg that has gone to sleep, it means no feeling in the body. If it is about shock or bad news, it means no feeling in the mind for a while. Try swapping in "could not feel" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Numb means not able to feel anything, in a body part or in a person.
fact: To numb means to make a part of the body lose feeling, as numbing cream does.
fact: Useful phrases: go numb, numb with cold, numb with shock.
fact: «Frostbite» makes skin white or greyish and numb, usually on fingers, toes, ears and nose.
fact: If your fingers or toes go numb and white in the cold, get somewhere warm, warm them gently in warm water (not hot), and tell an adult. Never rub them with snow or hold them by a fire.
exercise: «For a filling the dentist numbs the tooth with an injection.» What does numbs mean here? | *To make a part of the body lose feeling | To make a tooth shiny and bright | To make a loud noise | To make a tooth grow back
exercise: After the bad news, Maya sat still and said nothing. «She was numb with shock.» What does numb mean here? | Feeling very happy and excited | Feeling very hot and sweaty | Feeling a sudden tickle | *Feeling nothing for a while
exercise: Which phrase means your hands have lost feeling because of the cold? | Loud as thunder | Hot as toast | Glad with joy | *Numb with cold
test: «Frostbite makes skin white or greyish and numb.» Where is frostbite usually found? | Knees and elbows | Hair and eyebrows | *Fingers, toes, ears and nose | Back and shoulders
test: Your fingers have gone numb and white in the snow. What should you do? | Hold them close to a fire | Rub them hard with snow | Keep playing until they feel better | *Warm them gently and tell an adult
exam: «His lip felt fat and numb for a few hours after the injection.» What is the best meaning of numb here? | *A part of the body that cannot feel anything | A loud noise in the ear | A bright light in the eyes | A part of the body that is very hot
